#: includes/abilities/meta.php:96
msgid "The post-meta key to read. Must be on the operator's post-meta allowlist (or the allow-all wildcard) and not explicitly denied or hard-blocked; protected (underscore-prefixed), auth, and capability keys can never be exposed. A key that fails any of those checks is rejected before the read runs, not returned empty. Attachment alt text is stored under _wp_attachment_image_alt, a protected key, so it is never readable here. Call aafm-get-media-item, which returns alt as a plain field. The featured image is stored under _thumbnail_id, also protected; call aafm-get-post or aafm-get-page, which return the \"featured_image\" object."
msgstr ""

