msgid "Rate limit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:523
msgid "Per minute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:527
msgid "Rate limit, per minute"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:529
msgid "How many agent calls one connection can make per minute. Off by default (0), so nothing is capped until you set a number here. If you are not sure where to start, 60 is a reasonable limit for a single connected agent. Developers can also set this with the aafm_rate_limit_per_min filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:537
msgid "Before you save a list with anything in it, add the IP address your AI client connects from. As soon as this list has one entry, any request from an address that is not on it is blocked, including your own agent. Get it wrong and every agent call stops."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:542
msgid "IP allowlist"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:543
msgid "One per line"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:547
msgid "IP allowlist, one per line"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:548
msgid "One IP address or CIDR range per line. Leave it empty to allow connections from anywhere. When you save, any line that is not a valid IP or range is dropped."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:556
msgid "Force draft on create"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:558
msgid "Save the content an agent creates as a draft, no matter what status the request asked for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:559
msgid "Turn this on if you want to look over agent-created content before it goes live. Covers posts, pages, custom content items, reusable blocks, and WooCommerce products. Things without a draft state (media, menus, terms, comments, users, coupons, orders) and product variations are not affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:567
msgid "Strict block validation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:569
msgid "Reject an agent write when its block markup would show as invalid content in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:570
msgid "When this is off (the default), a write with questionable block markup still saves, and the agent is sent a warning so it can fix its next attempt. Turn it on to refuse the write instead, so nothing that could look broken in the editor is ever stored."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:577
msgid "Maximum title length"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:578
msgid "Characters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:582
msgid "Maximum title length, in characters"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:584
msgid "The longest title, in characters, an agent can set. Set it to 0 to leave the limit off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:591
msgid "Keep activity log for"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:592
msgid "Days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:596
msgid "Keep activity log for, in days"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:598
msgid "How many days of activity to keep. A daily cleanup removes anything older. Set it to 0 to keep every entry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:609
msgid "Permanently remove all plugin data when the plugin is deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:610
msgid "When this is off (the default), your settings, activity log, and OAuth data are kept if you delete the plugin, so a reinstall picks up your configuration. Turn it on only if you want everything removed. This cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:612
msgid "See more about deleting data on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:613
msgid "Either way, uninstalling this plugin never revokes an agent's access on its own. It never removes the dedicated agent user or any Application Password issued to it, since those are ordinary WordPress account credentials the plugin does not own. To cut off an agent, revoke its OAuth grant on the Connection tab, or delete its Application Password or user account from the Users screen, before or after you remove the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:618
msgid "Delete data on uninstall"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:627
msgid "Safety controls"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:634
msgid "These controls change how agent requests behave. Test a connection after you change anything here so you do not lock yourself out or quietly drop valid requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:646
msgid "Save settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:660
msgid "Danger zone"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/settings.php:664
